aiproof (0.1.18) unstable; urgency=medium

  * clipboard.save() now reads text with a single wl-paste call instead of
    asking --list-types first: measured 1192 ms -> 161 ms per proofread on a
    busy desktop, where each wl-paste spawn costs 200-600 ms. The type
    listing is only consulted when the text read fails (image or empty).
  * The paste flow logs per-step timings at DEBUG (app-detect,
    clipboard-save, clipboard-clear, settle+ctrl-c, poll-for-copy,
    clipboard-set, ctrl-v, restore-clipboard). Measuring real runs showed
    the capture/paste plumbing costing ~2.5s against a ~2.8s model call, so
    it needed to be as visible in the log as the model time already was.

